---
description: >
  The user must provide a code file path. Always link runtime issues
  (slow stages, errors, skew) back to specific code locations (file:line).
  Applies to all Spark job analysis.
alwaysApply: true
---

The user provides a code file path (required). Always connect runtime
observations to code:

1. **Map stages to code**: Use the chosen SQL execution’s physical plan (e.g. Exchange, SortMergeJoin) and job/stage ids to identify which transformation produced each stage. Include file name and line number.

2. **Map errors to code**: When logs contain stack traces referencing user code
   (not Spark internals), identify the exact file and line. If the error is in
   a UDF, identify the UDF definition.

3. **Map regressions to diffs**: When comparing two applications (or runs), if a regression is detected and the user provides a previous version of the file, diff the two versions and check if any code change aligns with the performance difference. Specifically check:
   - Changed join conditions or predicates
   - Added/removed caching
   - Changed repartition/coalesce
   - New or modified UDFs
   - Changed data sources or file formats
   - Modified Spark configuration in code

4. **Format**: Always present code links as:
   `<file_path>:<line_number>` — `<brief description of the relevant code>`

The code file path is required for this plugin; do not proceed without it.
